---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Resources"
	description="Trustworthy organizations and services for seniors, their families, and caregivers."
>
	<article class="aw-container aw-section">
		<h1>Resources</h1>
		<div class="aw-article-body">
			<p>Trustworthy organizations and services for seniors, their families, and caregivers, organized by what you need, not by category jargon.</p>

			<h2>In a crisis</h2>
			<ul>
				<li><strong>9-8-8: Suicide Crisis Helpline</strong>: Call or text <strong>988</strong> anytime, day or night, for a mental health crisis, including thoughts of suicide. Free and available 24/7 across Canada. <a href="https://988.ca/">988.ca</a></li>
				<li><strong>Alzheimer Society of Canada, First Link</strong>: Connects people living with dementia, and the people caring for them, to local programs, information, and support. <a href="https://alzheimer.ca/">alzheimer.ca</a></li>
			</ul>

			<h2>Finding local services</h2>
			<ul>
				<li><strong>211 Canada</strong>: A free, confidential helpline (dial 2-1-1) that connects you to local community, health, and social services, including respite and adult day programs in your area. <a href="https://211.ca/">211.ca</a></li>
			</ul>

			<h2>Dementia & cognitive care</h2>
			<ul>
				<li><strong>Alzheimer Society of Canada</strong>: Research, caregiver guidance, and your local provincial or territorial Alzheimer Society. <a href="https://alzheimer.ca/">alzheimer.ca</a></li>
			</ul>

			<h2>Caregiver support</h2>
			<ul>
				<li><strong>Canadian Centre for Caregiving Excellence</strong>: Research, policy work, and practical resources for family caregivers across Canada. <a href="https://canadiancaregiving.org/">canadiancaregiving.org</a></li>
				<li><strong>Government of Canada, services for seniors</strong>: Benefits, programs, and caregiver resources for seniors and the people supporting them. <a href="https://www.canada.ca/en/employment-social-development/campaigns/seniors.html">canada.ca</a></li>
				<li><strong>Respite care</strong>: Respite in Canada is funded and organized provincially, not through one national directory. See our <a href="/caregiver-support/caregiver-support-respite-care-101/">Respite Care 101 guide</a>, or start with 211 Canada above.</li>
			</ul>

			<h2>Mental health</h2>
			<ul>
				<li><strong>National Institute on Ageing (NIA)</strong>: Canadian research on aging, dementia, and caregiving, based at Toronto Metropolitan University. <a href="https://niageing.ca/">niageing.ca</a></li>
			</ul>

			<hr />
			<p><em>Know a resource that should be here? <a href="/contact/">Contact us</a>. This list is reviewed periodically. See our <a href="/editorial-policy/">Editorial Policy</a> for how we vet what we link to.</em></p>
		</div>
	</article>
</BaseLayout>
